speechtext:
This clause says that:
(a) any payment of money belonging to, or deposited or held to the credit of or for the benefit of, a maritime union, members of a maritime union, or the building corporation, where inadequate valuable consideration has been given therefor;
-is voidable if done, made or entered into on or after the 6th day of July, 1963. I should like to ask the minister two questions arising out of this wording. Will the trustees collect union dues from the members and, if so, would the trustees have the right to expel members for non-payment of dues?
